-- title:
--   Idelic first-inequality data for cyclic extensions of degree dividing 24
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ an extension of $K$ that is Galois with cyclic Galois group $L \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]} L$, suppose $[L:K]$ divides $24$, and let $\mathfrak f$ be an arbitrary ideal of $\mathcal O_K$ (no nonvanishing is assumed). The conclusion `IdeleFirstIneqDataAt K L 𝔣` asserts the existence of a group homomorphism $N$ from the idele units of $L$ to the idele units of $K$ with four properties. First, compatibility with adjusters: whenever $u$ is an idele of $L$ and $\alpha \in L^\times$ satisfies `IsAdjuster` at the extended modulus $\mathfrak f\mathcal O_L$ — i.e. the finite part of $u\alpha^{-1}$ has valuation $1$ at every finite place dividing the modulus and is congruent to $1$ there to the precision $\exp(-m_w)$ given by the multiplicity $m_w$ of that place in the modulus, and $\mathrm{archSign}$ holds for $u\alpha^{-1}$ at every real embedding of $L$ — then $N(u)$ and $\mathrm{Nm}_{L/K}(\alpha)$ satisfy `IsAdjuster` at $\mathfrak f$ over $K$. Secondly, content compatibility: for every idele $u$ of $L$, the fractional-ideal content $\prod_v \mathfrak p_v^{\mathrm{ord}_v}$ of the finite part of $N(u)$ equals `fracRelNormUnit`, the map sending each prime of $L$ to the prime below it raised to its inertia degree, applied to the content of the finite part of $u$. Thirdly, surjectivity at admissible level: if $\mathfrak f \ne \bot$ and $v^{\mathrm{admissibleExp}\ K\ v}$ divides $\mathfrak f$ for every finite place $v$ of $K$ whose prime above in $L$ has nontrivial inertia, then the subgroup `unitIdeles K 𝔣` — ideles that are local units at all finite places, congruent to $1$ modulo $\mathfrak f$ to the stated precision at the places dividing $\mathfrak f$, and of positive sign at all real embeddings — lies in the range of $N$. Fourthly, $[L:K]$ divides the index of the subgroup generated by the principal ideles of $K$ together with the range of $N$.
--
--   This packages the first inequality of global class field theory for a cyclic extension (the degree divides the norm index in the idele class group) together with the ray-class congruence and content compatibilities in which it is consumed; only the existence of some homomorphism with these properties is asserted, the intended one being the idelic norm of $L/K$. It feeds the construction of the Artin symbol and of transfer data for cyclic extensions of degree dividing $24$ in the Langlands–Tunnell part of the argument.
